{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00525",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 6.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Margaret Pemberton? Date of birth the fourth of March, nineteen fifty-one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.18,
      "end_seconds": 17.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "That's me. I've brought my diary, if that's all right. I've been writing it down since the start."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.14,
      "end_seconds": 26.21,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "Brilliant, that saves time. Leg cramps, I see from the booking. Walk me through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.6,
      "end_seconds": 42.24,
      "duration_seconds": 14.64,
      "text": "Right. I get terrible cramps in my calves at night, mostly the left, waking me up around two in the morning. They've been going on for six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.19,
      "end_seconds": 46.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Six weeks. How often, according to the diary?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.73,
      "end_seconds": 57.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.44,
      "text": "Let me see. Three or four nights a week. Last week it was four, Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.49,
      "end_seconds": 62.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "How bad are they when they hit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.11,
      "end_seconds": 78.42,
      "duration_seconds": 14.31,
      "text": "Severe. I have to get out of bed and stand on the cold floor. I'd put it at eight out of ten, and there's a sore ache left behind the next day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.97,
      "end_seconds": 84.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Anything that sets them off, anything that helps?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.57,
      "end_seconds": 95.34,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "They're worse after a day of gardening. Stretching the calf against the wall is the only thing that eases it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.72,
      "end_seconds": 101.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Good detail. Anything else going on with the legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.41,
      "end_seconds": 110.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.53,
      "text": "My ankles swell by the evening. And I'm tired, a heavy sort of tired, which is new since the autumn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.18,
      "end_seconds": 122.84,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "Swollen ankles and tiredness, noted. Now, a few safety questions. Any chest pain, or shortness of breath on the stairs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.02,
      "end_seconds": 132.06,
      "duration_seconds": 8.04,
      "text": "No chest pain. No shortness of breath either, I did the stairs at the library yesterday without any trouble."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.92,
      "end_seconds": 139.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Good. Any numbness in the legs, or weakness, like your leg giving way?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.19,
      "end_seconds": 145.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "No numbness, and no weakness. Just the cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.23,
      "end_seconds": 152.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Right. Tablets. What are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.89,
      "end_seconds": 166.96,
      "duration_seconds": 13.07,
      "text": "The amlodipine, 5 mg once a day in the morning, for the blood pressure. And the water tablet, furosemide, 40 mg, once a day as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.53,
      "end_seconds": 172.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Okay, and do you take them every day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.03,
      "end_seconds": 180.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Every morning, regularly, without fail. I have a pill box with the days on it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.09,
      "end_seconds": 183.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Good. Any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.58,
      "end_seconds": 194.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.14,
      "text": "Penicillin. I get a rash, it came up all over my chest when I was about thirty. I've avoided it ever since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.86,
      "end_seconds": 204.12,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "Penicillin and a rash, I'll flag that. Any other medical conditions apart from the blood pressure?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.74,
      "end_seconds": 209.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Osteoarthritis in my knees. And migraines, though they stopped after the menopause."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.27,
      "end_seconds": 214.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Blood pressure, osteoarthritis, migraines. Any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.42,
      "end_seconds": 227.29,
      "duration_seconds": 10.87,
      "text": "The gallbladder came out about ten years ago. And I had a right knee replacement in 2019, which was a great success."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.84,
      "end_seconds": 232.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "And in the family, any big illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.15,
      "end_seconds": 240.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "My father had a stroke. My mother had type 2 diabetes for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.92,
      "end_seconds": 244.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Thank you. Do you smoke or drink?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.73,
      "end_seconds": 258.79,
      "duration_seconds": 13.06,
      "text": "I stopped smoking twenty years ago. A glass of wine with dinner, no more. I'm a retired teacher, so I'm very good at following rules."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.58,
      "end_seconds": 266.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "That makes my job easier. Any trouble with your waterworks, passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.6,
      "end_seconds": 276.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "No, that's all normal. Although I notice the water tablet makes me go a lot in the morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.61,
      "end_seconds": 285.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Expected with that tablet. I'll do your observations and then take a look at your legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.77,
      "end_seconds": 317.09,
      "duration_seconds": 12.32,
      "text": "Blood pressure is 148 over 86. Pulse 72 beats per minute. Temperature 36.6 degrees. Oxygen saturation 97 percent. And your weight is 78 kilograms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.08,
      "end_seconds": 326.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "My blood pressure is usually a bit lower than that at home. I've got those numbers in the diary too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.98,
      "end_seconds": 344.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "I'll look at the diary afterwards. Lie back, I'm checking both lower legs now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.49,
      "end_seconds": 367.11,
      "duration_seconds": 9.62,
      "text": "There's mild swelling around both ankles. No redness or warmth in either calf, and the pulses at the feet are present."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.95,
      "end_seconds": 369.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Is that good?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.07,
      "end_seconds": 386.84,
      "duration_seconds": 14.77,
      "text": "Reassuring. Here's my thinking. The cramps are most likely related to your water tablet, which can wash out potassium and magnesium. But I can't rule out a circulation problem in the legs as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.76,
      "end_seconds": 390.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "And the swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.95,
      "end_seconds": 402.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.41,
      "text": "Amlodipine can cause some of that too, so it may be both tablets. I'm not changing anything today until I have bloods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.86,
      "end_seconds": 405.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.19,
      "end_seconds": 418.4,
      "duration_seconds": 12.21,
      "text": "I'd like to order a blood test for your potassium and kidney function, and a separate magnesium level. You can have both done this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.79,
      "end_seconds": 421.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Fine. Fasting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.26,
      "end_seconds": 433.43,
      "duration_seconds": 11.17,
      "text": "No need. I'll also arrange an ECG, because low potassium can affect the heart rhythm. The nurse can do it straight after the bloods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.0,
      "end_seconds": 440.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Is there anything about my heart I should worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.5,
      "end_seconds": 454.9,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "Nothing that I've heard or seen so far. This is to be careful. If the swelling doesn't settle, we'll consider an ultrasound scan of the leg veins."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 455.88,
      "end_seconds": 457.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "All right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 458.64,
      "end_seconds": 468.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "For the cramps themselves, stretch the calves before bed, keep your fluids up through the day, and bring the diary next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 468.87,
      "end_seconds": 483.26,
      "duration_seconds": 14.39,
      "text": "I'll add a column for the stretching. And I wanted to mention, looking at the diary again, I did actually miss the amlodipine on Tuesday and Thursday last week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 485.27,
      "end_seconds": 495.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.11,
      "text": "Thanks for being honest. Try to take it with breakfast every morning so it's tied to something. Don't double up when you miss one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 497.4,
      "end_seconds": 498.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "Noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 500.32,
      "end_seconds": 505.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "I'll see you again in ten days to go through the results."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 506.83,
      "end_seconds": 511.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Ten days. I'll make the appointment at the desk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 513.85,
      "end_seconds": 517.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Good. Off you go to the lab."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 518.42,
      "end_seconds": 520.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 523.04,
      "end_seconds": 524.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Goodbye, Mrs Pemberton."
    }
  ]
}
